{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WNTWVNeiLwPR7MQL1NGYfU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"\n     2→Cross-chapter character consensus builder.\n     3→\n     4→Merges character proposals across chapters, resolves aliases,\n     5→and produces the final CharacterMap.\n     6→\"\"\"\n     7→\n     8→import re\n     9→import hashlib\n    10→import time\n    11→from typing import Optional, Iterable\n    12→from collections import defaultdict\n    13→from difflib import SequenceMatcher\n    14→import logging\n    15→\n    16→from .models import (\n    17→    CharacterProposal,\n    18→    CharacterValidationResult,\n    19→    Character,\n    20→    CharacterMap,\n    21→    CharacterMention,\n    22→    CharacterType,\n    23→)\n    24→from .constants import are_potential_nicknames, get_nickname_variants\n    25→from ..llm import LLMClient\n    26→\n    27→logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    28→\n    29→# Character classification prompts\n    30→CHARACTER_TYPE_SYSTEM = \"\"\"You are a literary analyst classifying character types.\n    31→\n    32→Classify each character as one of:\n    33→- STORY: An active participant in the narrative who appears in scenes, speaks dialogue, or takes actions\n    34→- HISTORICAL: A real historical figure mentioned in passing (e.g., Napoleon, Einstein)\n    35→- REFERENCED: A fictional character from other works mentioned in passing (e.g., Hamlet, Sherlock Holmes)\n    36→\n    37→Return ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\"\"\"\n    38→\n    39→CHARACTER_TYPE_PROMPT = \"\"\"Classify this character's role in the narrative.\n    40→\n    41→CHARACTER: {name}\n    42→MENTION COUNT: {mention_count}\n    43→CHAPTERS PRESENT: {chapters}\n    44→SAMPLE CONTEXTS:\n    45→{contexts}\n    46→\n    47→Based on the contexts, determine if this character:\n    48→1. Actively participates (speaks, acts, appears in scenes) → STORY\n    49→2. Is a real historical figure mentioned in passing → HISTORICAL\n    50→3. Is a fictional character from other works → REFERENCED\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3924aa2c-d6fe-4686-86bb-94b756a35690","uuid":"b548ad53-cce5-455b-9088-081303346c0c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py","content":"\"\"\"\nCross-chapter character consensus builder.\n\nMerges character proposals across chapters, resolves aliases,\nand produces the final CharacterMap.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\nimport hashlib\nimport time\nfrom typing import Optional, Iterable\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom difflib import SequenceMatcher\nimport logging\n\nfrom .models import (\n    CharacterProposal,\n    CharacterValidationResult,\n    Character,\n    CharacterMap,\n    CharacterMention,\n    CharacterType,\n)\nfrom .constants import are_potential_nicknames, get_nickname_variants\nfrom ..llm import LLMClient\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# Character classification prompts\nCHARACTER_TYPE_SYSTEM = \"\"\"You are a literary analyst classifying character types.\n\nClassify each character as one of:\n- STORY: An active participant in the narrative who appears in scenes, speaks dialogue, or takes actions\n- HISTORICAL: A real historical figure mentioned in passing (e.g., Napoleon, Einstein)\n- REFERENCED: A fictional character from other works mentioned in passing (e.g., Hamlet, Sherlock Holmes)\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\"\"\"\n\nCHARACTER_TYPE_PROMPT = \"\"\"Classify this character's role in the narrative.\n\nCHARACTER: {name}\nMENTION COUNT: {mention_count}\nCHAPTERS PRESENT: {chapters}\nSAMPLE CONTEXTS:\n{contexts}\n\nBased on the contexts, determine if this character:\n1. Actively participates (speaks, acts, appears in scenes) → STORY\n2. Is a real historical figure mentioned in passing → HISTORICAL\n3. Is a fictional character from other works → REFERENCED","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2336}}}
